<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire hits Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53989d3139d3dc60a7d8fcb454d7633171461a041f90664bf103f2b8308da8bc</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--07c7cd5dbdea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fire at a confectionery factory in Indonesia's Banten province has killed at least three people. Dozens are also unaccounted for after the blaze, which destroyed large parts of the facility.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Indonesia sign trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9809cfc45b1bc4e91e147f466e1b42d8381b825dc39fec5219f42f89eb28548</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099--bb068ad239d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A deal covering 730 million people promises lower tariffs and new investment opportunities as the European Union seeks to diversify trade ties amid growing global economic tensions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nepal PM Balendra Shah to arrive in Delhi for first visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f7e2ff32467325b702057d0e19306a60ea036d6c9326d0fac05345fe5707473</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-to-arrive-in-delhi-for-first-visit/live-80008104--e2d860834e27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-to-arrive-in-delhi-for-first-visit/live-80008104?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rapper-turned-prime minister Balendra Shah is in New Delhi for his first bilateral visit since taking office, with talks with Modi expected to focus on flood reconstruction aid, trade and energy. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f08b81c93b94c69efd72d108ea5eb84f91dc22565b263b4e4a8a78379de5e26b</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar genocide ruling: Rohingya say struggle for justice not over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b2d101642fe7bab9035e8653e5ee8706e0c012ee79fba5c2fa9476ac0e9746b</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365--347a55d37759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ has held Myanmar responsible for genocide against the Rohingya and ordered restitution and reparations. Community members have hailed the ruling, but caution that achieving real change will be long and hard.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5d9b6125e17cd56fed8a63c7ad246e37603a64e80263920b52a1073cd3a2152</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>India: Pakistani minister visits Delhi for SCO forum amid frozen ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5794a2a08849289a3223daa0a367516bf20baba83d87b43a0c0d2c329ef881</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264--d096d9f0fd84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Malik has arrived in New Delhi for an SCO cultural forum, the first visit by a Pakistani federal minister since 2023. Meanwhile, Cyclone Akvan has made landfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi praises 'turnaround' in relationship with Australia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47f7a3f6dadae88199246414036ec86124b3f55aa8a5926ba45647fb2ff4482a</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229--091456c7e1ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The leaders of Australia and China have held talks on sidelines of APEC summit. Australian PM Anthony Albanese is also slated to meet Chinese Premier Li Qiang.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin have held trilateral talks ― but what did they achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4a042768661bddd5fb55184d575440ad21b819a35fb56ec697afad958fe3f4f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-have-held-trilateral-talks-_-but-what-did-they-achieve/a-79996668--6af4ec68160a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-have-held-trilateral-talks-―-but-what-did-they-achieve/a-79996668?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The presidents of China, the US and Russia have held an unprecedented summit. While Trump said the three leaders were "making history," Xi described the talks as "fruitful" and Putin called them "open and candid."</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f23084f70e15045c38c90d9620f3e48e3b151aa8b24fbffc3df3dd43fe5d921</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China faces Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2b14490249e0b6885f377f21b3b84b934bb41c3bcf7a4a1c35fe5b5326d5a5</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--86131bd0e961.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Russia, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
